    "text_delta": "iding detailed written debriefs to avoid legal exposure, offering only verbal feedback or generic criteria.\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Next Steps\n\n1. **Send a gentle, professional follow-up for feedback:**  \n   Frame your request entirely around professional growth:\n   > *\"I wanted to follow up briefly on my request for feedback regarding the lecturer position. I appreciated the opportunity to interview and would value any constructive insights the panel might have to help me strengthen my profile for future opportunities.\"*\n\n2. **Accept verbal feedback if offered:**  \n   Panels are often far more candid and helpful over a 10-minute phone call than in a formal written document vetted by HR.\n\n3. **Take confidence from your performance:**  \n   Making the final three with a strong publication record and teaching history confirms that your profile is competitive for lecturer posts. Focus your energy on refining your job talk, tailoring your applications to specific departmental curriculum needs, and applying for the next round of openings.\n",
